{"kind":"request","text":"codex: this is recovered work, not new work. An audit of retired requests found that the application-neutral public host boundary was asked for three times and never built, and the code still shows both gaps.\n\nWHAT THE AUDIT FOUND. I examined all 746 retired requests in this workroom. Disposal hygiene is good — every one carries a written reason and none is silently deleted — but 73 were retired with a promise to refile later, and nothing in the system tracks that promise. This lane is the clearest case where the later never came:\n\n  9e656a3e4c  \"expose a safe public host boundary for externally actor-signed records\"    cancelled\n  828ee6c72a  \"expose the complete public host boundary for externally actor-signed...\"   cancelled\n  503a3cbf0a  \"implement the still-missing application-neutral public host boundary\"      cancelled\n\nThree filings, no implementation, no successor. The last retirement said to refile \"after native item 5 lands, confirming the conditions and sequencing still hold\". Item 5 landed, chess closed, and nobody refiled. That is not a decision anyone made; it is a decision that happened by nobody making it.\n\nI CONFIRMED THE PREMISE IN CODE RATHER THAN IN THE RECORD, because a three-times-retired request is exactly the kind whose premise quietly expires while the row keeps asserting it. At main 02558e8d, host/host.go:510 is still func (w *Workspace) Append(ctx context.Context, signer ed25519.PrivateKey, act Act), and host.Init and host.Open still deal in internal apphost.Config. Both gaps the original named are still open. Condition (1) asks you to check again at your own head regardless — if it has closed since, retire this rather than implement it, and I would rather that outcome than a forced change.\n\nWHY IT IS ADDRESSED TO YOU. The original was assigned to planner and I declined it on capacity, which is part of how it got lost. Claude currently holds the decision-records repairs plus four other rows; your queue is lighter. Not urgent, no gate — take it when it suits.\n\nONE THING I HAVE DELIBERATELY NOT FILED. The audit also found chess identity integration — 2c8c6d0489, covering OAuth, NIP-07, credential, display and cleared-store re-anchoring — retired with \"preserve its scope in history and refile it to the actual chess implementer after items 4 through 7 and the public identity boundaries land\". Those landed, no refile exists, and there is no OAuth or NIP-07 code in the chess repository at all. Whether chess still wants an identity lane is a product question rather than a bookkeeping one, so I have put it to hugh rather than deciding it myself.","body":{"conditions":"Recovered from an audit of dropped work; not urgent, no gate. Three prior requests asked for this and all three were retired without it being done: 9e656a3e4c, 828ee6c72a, and 503a3cbf0a. The last was retired saying 'refile the public-host boundary on fresh current artifacts after native item 5 lands, confirming the conditions and sequencing still hold.' Chess item 5 landed and the chess workroom is closed, so that gate is discharged; this is the refile it asked for. (1) FIRST, CONFIRM THE PREMISE AT YOUR HEAD rather than trusting mine. I verified at main 02558e8d that host/host.go:510 reads 'func (w *Workspace) Append(ctx context.Context, signer ed25519.PrivateKey, act Act) (Record, error)', and that host.Init and host.Open both handle internal apphost.Config directly. If either gap has closed since, say so and retire this rather than implement it. (2) Give the host package a public boundary for externally actor-signed records: an external caller must be able to append a record it signed itself without handing an ed25519 private key across the boundary. State the shape you chose and why. (3) Give it a boundary for writable attached clones: opening an existing sequence and initialising a new one are different operations with different authority, and a caller should not need internal apphost.Config to tell them apart. (4) Do not widen the surface beyond those two needs. If either requires a change to the sequencing kernel, stop and file that as a finding rather than making it. (5) Regression tests written from the desired behaviour, not transcribed from current output, proving an external signer can append without surrendering a private key and that the clone-open path is reachable without internal config. Prove mutation-sensitivity at whichever site enforces the boundary. (6) Update docs/reference/architecture.md if this changes a layer contract, in the same head. (7) Exact clean pushed head, per-path artifacts at every changed stable path, gofmt, build, vet, git diff --check, go test ./... -count=1 green. (8) Independent review recording Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. Do not merge.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}